diff --git a/NGX-STACK-EXPERIMENT.md b/NGX-STACK-EXPERIMENT.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7662f64
--- /dev/null
+++ b/NGX-STACK-EXPERIMENT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# Experimental direct NGX DLSS-G + NVIDIA NGX Frame Warp
+
+This experiment combines **two actual NVIDIA NGX features** in the JustFlow
+presenter: direct-NGX DLSS Frame Generation (`NVSDK_NGX_Feature_FrameGeneration`)
+and NGX Frame Warp (`NVSDK_NGX_Feature_Reserved15`). Each presented real or
+generated frame can be registered and warped, subject to a strict quality gate.
+
+It is *not* an official NVIDIA Reflex 2 implementation and is **not yet a V39
+port**. It uses JustFlow's WGC/DXGI capture rather than V39's NvFBC PID CUDA
+capture and does not claim V39's NvOFA confidence-cost handling or Preset C.
+
+The first experiment is specifically intended to determine whether direct NGX
+DLSS-G and the NGX Frame Warp feature coexist on a real RTX 50-series GPU.
+
+## Strict quality settings
+
+- Real input samples only: recorded raw mouse deltas up to the current refresh;
+  no guesses about future mouse input.
+- Camera fit must have R² >= 0.92 and >= 40 observations.
+- Capture-to-warp age <= 60 ms.
+- Horizontal/vertical warp vector is clipped to 2 output pixels total.
+- No-warp mask is built using the existing optical-flow path; recorded HUD
+  rectangles are copied back after warp.
+- A failed Frame Warp feature creation or evaluation is logged and causes the
+  experimental pipeline to stop. No shader fallback is labelled Reflex 2.
+- Valid calibrations with less than 0.35 pixel of motion skip the warp entirely.
+
+## Runtime files
+
+Place `nvngx_dlssg.dll` and `nvngx_latewarp.dll` (NVIDIA signed runtimes,
+**not included in the public build**) next to `justflow.exe`.
+Use `RUN-NGX-STACK-CS2.cmd` for CS2; this sets `JF_NGX_STACK_LW=1`.
+Keep the original V39 application separate and compare latency with the
+experiment. The NVIDIA feature may reject this combination or add latency.
+
+## Testing
+
+1. Start CS2 in borderless windowed mode at 1920x1080.
+2. Run `RUN-NGX-STACK-CS2.cmd`.
+3. Confirm log messages report *both* NGX DLSS-G and `feature created` for
+   Latewarp. Then move the mouse for camera-fit calibration.
+4. Only after the log shows `NGX Frame Warp applied to real+generated output`
+   should the experiment be considered active.
+5. Compare latency against V39 at the same base and displayed FPS. Do not use
+   this in anti-cheat games before checking their overlay policies.
+
+## License
+
+Derived from [JustFlow](https://github.com/wealdly/JustFlow) by wealdly,
+copyright (c) 2026, licensed MIT. Retain the repository's LICENSE and NOTICE.
